Falsifies `interfaces_note::interface_verification::a_decoded_interface_list_encodes_back_to_its_bytes`.

The defect: `decode_interfaces` rejects a decreasing id (`p > id`) but lets a
repeated id through, where the contract is strictly ascending, each once. A list
with a duplicate then decodes, and re-encoding it trips the encoder's own
strictly-ascending assertion, so what the decoder accepted is not something the
encoder can spell: the one-encoding claim is broken.

Expected to fail: the `interface ids strictly ascend, each once` assertion inside
`encode_interfaces`, reached from the harness's last line, on any two-entry list
with equal ids.


